{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1503401139,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyNTE5MjQzODU=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1745","origin":"github"},"title":"Demo of a simple reproducible analysis on public data","message":"```sh\ndatalad create demo\ncd demo\n# obtain two public datasets as input\ndatalad install -d . -s ///openfmri/ds000001 inputs/ds000001\ndatalad install -d . -s ///openfmri/ds000002 inputs/ds000002\n# create a script that will perform brain extraction on any given\n# MRI file\nmkdir code\n\ncat \u003c\u003c EOT \u003e code/brain_extraction.sh\n# enable FSL\n. /etc/fsl/5.0/fsl.sh\n\n# obtain all inputs\ndatalad get \\$@\n# perform brain extraction\ncount=1\nfor nifti in \\$@; do\n  subdir=\"sub-\\$(printf %03d \\$count)\"\n  mkdir -p \\$subdir\n  bet \\$nifti \\$subdir/anat -m\n  count=\\$((count + 1)) \ndone\nEOT\n\n# save this version of the script in the dataset\ndatalad add code -m \"Brain extraction script\" --to-git\ndatalad save --version-tag setup_done\n# run the brain extraction script on the structural images\n# of the first subject from each dataset (could be all of them)\n# this saves the outcomes together with the exact command call\n# and version of the script\ndatalad run bash -e code/brain_extraction.sh inputs/ds*/sub-01/anat/sub-01_T1w.nii.gz\n# enough information is recorded to rerun the command, not that\n# the re-generated data is exactly the same and the dataset does not\n# need to be saved\ndatalad run --rerun\ndu -sh .\n# we can verify that our processing has not modified the inputs\ndatalad diff --revision setup_done inputs/*\n# hence we can uninstall them, they are public data after all\ndatalad uninstall inputs/*\ndu -sh .\n# however, all inputs are still available and can be re-obtained\n# on demand. For example, we can rerun our brain extraction command\n# again, and it will reobtain all required datasets to perform the\n# same operation that was originally recorded\n# note that it gets identical results, and the dataset does not need\n# to be saved\ndatalad run --rerun\n```","files":null}]}